# Lumora Gallery — root .htaccess
#
# Lumora Gallery needs no mod_rewrite rules of its own: every public URL is
# query-string based (?cat=N, ?album=N, ?view=...), so plain Apache file/
# directory resolution already serves every request correctly — index.php
# for the front page, admin/index.php for /admin/, install/index.php for
# /install/, and so on.
#
# This file exists only to STOP a parent directory's own RewriteEngine
# rules from reaching into a Lumora Gallery install that happens to sit
# in a subdirectory beneath an unrelated app (a common shared-hosting
# layout: e.g. domains/example.com/public_html/.htaccess belonging to a
# different app installed at the domain root, with Lumora Gallery living
# in domains/example.com/public_html/gallery/). Apache merges .htaccess
# files hierarchically from the filesystem root down to the file being
# served, so without this, an ancestor .htaccess's RewriteRule directives
# still apply here even though they were never written with Lumora
# Gallery's own directory layout in mind.
#
# Real-world case that prompted this file: a Lumora Press install's own
# root .htaccess deliberately excludes admin/ from its "serve real
# files/directories directly" rule (Press's own admin/ is meant to be
# routed through Press's front controller — see that project's
# DECISIONS.md), so requests fall through to Press's catch-all
# `RewriteRule ^ index.php`. When a Lumora Gallery install shared a
# parent directory with a Press install on the same domain, that same
# exclusion silently applied to Gallery's own admin/ too — a bare
# /admin/ request (no filename) was rewritten to Press's index.php and
# served the wrong app's homepage entirely, while /admin/index.php
# (an explicit filename, matched by the parent's earlier "-f" rule
# before the admin-specific exclusion) worked fine. `RewriteEngine Off`
# stops mod_rewrite processing for anything under this directory tree,
# restoring Apache's normal file/directory resolution regardless of
# what any ancestor .htaccess tries to rewrite.
<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
    RewriteEngine Off
</IfModule>

<FilesMatch "\.(ini|log|sh|sql|md)$">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>
